From e886794cc8cb77f610438f2271d5a787f13458fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:32:47 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Separate fax from calls, add a dashboard time zone, and make
 comparisons work

Call figures were distorted by three things in RingCentral's data:

- Faxes share the call log. They are now marked by the Worker and kept out of
  every call metric, with their own tile and Fax activity card.
- A single answer rate mixed outbound connects with inbound answers and did not
  count 'Accepted' (an answered inbound call). It is now two rates: inbound
  answered and outbound connected.
- Inbound calls nobody picked up carry no extension, so they were all
  'Unassigned'. They are now matched to the dialled number through the
  account's phone-number list.

Also:

- Days, hours and displayed times use one time zone: the RingCentral account's
  by default, or one picked in Settings. The heatmap shows the hours calls
  actually happen instead of a fixed 8am-6pm UTC window.
- The period before the selected one is imported in the background so 'vs prior
  period' has data; the prior window no longer skips a day; tiles say 'no prior
  data' when there is nothing to compare.
- Departments come from RingCentral's directory, with the Settings mapping as an
  override. With none set, charts rank team members instead of one
  'Unassigned' bar.
- Service level and abandon rate tiles appear only when queue data exists.
- SMS delivery rate is measured on messages sent, not on all messages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
